WEBVTT

00:01:30.400 --> 00:01:34.900
<b>Mystery 1 "The Limb Screen"</b>

00:01:33.030 --> 00:01:34.900
Fuzzy, go around the other side!

00:01:53.940 --> 00:01:58.720
Utakuni-dono, I understand your 
attachment to the mundane world.

00:01:59.220 --> 00:02:03.040
However, you can't remain here any longer.

00:02:03.040 --> 00:02:05.220
You must prepare to leave.

00:02:13.160 --> 00:02:15.300
Please let me exorcise you.

00:02:15.300 --> 00:02:19.300
In the Underworld, 
you won't be alone anymore.

00:02:21.260 --> 00:02:22.420
Are you ready?

00:02:24.060 --> 00:02:27.500
Master of the Mononokean, Abeno Haruitsuki,

00:02:27.500 --> 00:02:29.980
requesting a portal to the Underworld.

00:02:39.260 --> 00:02:41.060
Take care!

00:02:54.140 --> 00:02:55.260
Ashiya.

00:02:55.260 --> 00:02:56.070
Yes.

00:02:57.240 --> 00:02:58.530
Here's today's pay.

00:02:58.940 --> 00:03:00.800
Is this all?

00:03:00.800 --> 00:03:01.420
What?

00:03:01.420 --> 00:03:02.880
But Abeno-san...

00:03:02.880 --> 00:03:07.300
I know I failed to catch him in the end, 
but I worked really hard today!

00:03:07.300 --> 00:03:08.910
You should be paying me in bills!

00:03:08.910 --> 00:03:11.860
What? You just didn't make 
any dumb screw-ups, that's all.

00:03:11.860 --> 00:03:13.420
And stop looking so smug.

00:03:13.420 --> 00:03:17.360
At this rate, I'll never be able 
to pay off the debt I owe you!

00:03:17.360 --> 00:03:18.200
Shut up!

00:03:18.200 --> 00:03:20.900
We exorcised the yokai. The job is done.

00:03:20.900 --> 00:03:22.050
Let's go.

00:03:25.500 --> 00:03:31.310
By the way, didn't you tell that 
yokai he wouldn't be alone anymore?

00:03:32.280 --> 00:03:34.440
He's like the hairball.

00:03:34.440 --> 00:03:38.400
He was a pet that became a yokai after dying.

00:03:40.120 --> 00:03:42.020
I see.

00:03:42.020 --> 00:03:45.460
He missed people, so he haunted them.

00:03:45.460 --> 00:03:47.900
And each time, his body grew larger.

00:03:48.800 --> 00:03:50.910
If we'd waited any longer to exorcise him,

00:03:51.320 --> 00:03:54.400
he would've been too big to fit 
through an Underworld portal.

00:03:56.720 --> 00:04:00.740
Hey, Abeno-san... I have a request.

00:04:05.340 --> 00:04:06.930
<b>Lose One Turn</b>

00:04:09.440 --> 00:04:12.430
Fuzzy, why don't we call it here?

00:04:12.430 --> 00:04:14.520
We've played a lot of ball games already.

00:04:14.520 --> 00:04:16.280
Let's do something different next.

00:04:16.280 --> 00:04:17.500
Give me a minute.

00:04:17.500 --> 00:04:19.440
I'm going to tidy up the room.

00:04:33.960 --> 00:04:35.660
<i>He's so happy.</i>

00:04:37.180 --> 00:04:41.300
<i>Fuzzy was originally like that 
yokai we exorcised today.</i>

00:04:41.860 --> 00:04:44.840
<i>Even after becoming a yokai, 
he remained in the mundane world.</i>

00:04:45.620 --> 00:04:47.340
<i>He wanted someone's attention.</i>

00:04:47.700 --> 00:04:52.700
<i>He happened to meet me and Abeno-san, 
two people who can see yokai,</i>

00:04:52.700 --> 00:04:56.540
<i>but most yokai are alone as long as 
they remain in the mundane world.</i>

00:04:56.540 --> 00:04:58.100
<i>Because I met Fuzzy,</i>

00:04:58.100 --> 00:05:03.020
<i>I owe Abeno-san a debt I don't 
know when I'll be able to repay,</i>

00:05:03.020 --> 00:05:05.580
<i>and I have frightening and 
dangerous experiences.</i>

00:05:07.380 --> 00:05:10.620
<i>But because I understand how the yokai feel,</i>

00:05:11.260 --> 00:05:13.820
<i>I want to keep doing this job forever.</i>

00:05:16.720 --> 00:05:20.130
Hanae! Hanae, are you 
planning to sleep all day?

00:05:23.880 --> 00:05:26.140
F-Fuzzy?!

00:05:26.140 --> 00:05:27.510
Oh, right.

00:05:28.120 --> 00:05:31.780
I asked Abeno-san to let 
you stay over last night.

00:05:32.320 --> 00:05:34.270
Come on, Fuzzy. Time to get up.

00:05:35.770 --> 00:05:37.180
See you later.

00:05:37.960 --> 00:05:41.360
You were making a lot of noise 
in your room last night.

00:05:41.360 --> 00:05:46.900
H-Huh?! I-I was just exercising, 
since I've gained a little weight...

00:05:46.900 --> 00:05:48.960
Have you?

00:05:49.580 --> 00:05:51.030
Oh, your shoulder...

00:05:52.910 --> 00:05:54.880
There was some lint on it.

00:05:55.420 --> 00:05:58.620
R-Really? Thanks.

00:05:58.620 --> 00:06:01.840
Are you sick again or something?

00:06:01.840 --> 00:06:04.240
The kids aren't calling you "Hanae-chan 
of the Nurse's Office," do they?

00:06:04.240 --> 00:06:06.960
How do you know about that nickname, Mom?

00:06:06.960 --> 00:06:08.520
Don't worry about me.

00:06:08.520 --> 00:06:10.640
I'm great. I feel really great now.

00:06:11.560 --> 00:06:12.760
Wh-What's that?

00:06:12.760 --> 00:06:14.360
Sorbus commixta.

00:06:14.360 --> 00:06:17.100
In the language of flowers, 
it means "I'm watching over you."

00:06:17.100 --> 00:06:20.200
Please stop using flowers 
to express yourself!

00:06:20.200 --> 00:06:22.200
I'll see you later.

00:06:22.200 --> 00:06:23.940
See you later.

00:06:25.440 --> 00:06:27.800
It's finally summer.

00:06:33.840 --> 00:06:35.840
So, summer vacation is approaching.

00:06:35.840 --> 00:06:38.620
This is your first summer 
vacation as high school students.

00:06:37.370 --> 00:06:49.760
Summer Vacation

00:06:38.620 --> 00:06:41.960
You might want to start planning 
now so you can enjoy

00:06:41.960 --> 00:06:44.320
a fulfilling high school summer vacation.

00:06:44.320 --> 00:06:47.360
I've already started planning 
my family vacation.

00:06:47.260 --> 00:06:50.620
Sir, you're rambling.

00:06:47.360 --> 00:06:48.900
I wanted to go to the mountains,

00:06:48.900 --> 00:06:51.820
but my daughter insisted 
on going to the beach.

00:06:51.820 --> 00:06:53.760
My adorable daughter...

00:07:01.080 --> 00:07:04.000
<i>I wonder where Abeno-san is.</i>

00:07:04.000 --> 00:07:06.840
<i>He didn't say we had work today.</i>

00:07:07.520 --> 00:07:09.320
<i>In any case, I need to return Fuzzy to...</i>

00:07:09.320 --> 00:07:10.490
Ashiyan!

00:07:10.740 --> 00:07:12.760
Oh, hey, Fusshi and Saga.

00:07:12.760 --> 00:07:15.820
What's wrong? You were 
staring at your shoulder.

00:07:15.820 --> 00:07:18.620
I-It's just a little stiff!

00:07:19.100 --> 00:07:21.740
Our teacher rambles way too much.

00:07:21.740 --> 00:07:24.250
Y-Yeah.

00:07:24.920 --> 00:07:27.080
Wanna stop by the convenience store?

00:07:27.080 --> 00:07:28.840
Let's get ice cream.

00:07:28.840 --> 00:07:32.090
Uh, sorry. I've got somewhere to go today.

00:07:38.960 --> 00:07:40.180
What was that?

00:07:40.180 --> 00:07:41.880
What's wrong, Ashiyan?

00:07:41.880 --> 00:07:44.020
Huh?! Oh, um...

00:07:44.520 --> 00:07:46.160
Hey, what's that?!

00:07:46.160 --> 00:07:46.700
Huh?

00:07:46.700 --> 00:07:48.360
Well, I've gotta hurry!

00:07:48.360 --> 00:07:52.140
Please don't suddenly connect the 
classroom door to the Mononokean!

00:07:52.140 --> 00:07:54.300
What did you skip school fo—

00:07:55.440 --> 00:07:57.380
SOS?!

00:07:59.020 --> 00:08:01.620
What is this? Is there trouble? 
Was there an accident?

00:08:01.620 --> 00:08:02.460
It's booze, isn't it?

00:08:02.460 --> 00:08:03.520
Someone's sick?!

00:08:03.520 --> 00:08:06.020
Is it acute alcohol-whatever-poisoning?

00:08:06.020 --> 00:08:07.680
There's no "whatever."

00:08:07.680 --> 00:08:08.660
Also, shut up.

00:08:08.660 --> 00:08:09.540
No, wait!

00:08:09.540 --> 00:08:11.440
The Mononokean has been drinking? How?!

00:08:09.880 --> 00:08:13.010
Look closely under the SOS.

00:08:11.440 --> 00:08:13.010
Isn't this room itself the Mononokean?!

00:08:13.440 --> 00:08:15.300
SOS...

00:08:16.440 --> 00:08:17.890
Partly cloudy?

00:08:17.890 --> 00:08:21.100
Mononokean, what does 
that mark actually mean?

00:08:21.930 --> 00:08:26.650
It's the crest of Newt Lake's Legislator.

00:08:26.650 --> 00:08:28.640
Thanks for spelling it out.

00:08:28.640 --> 00:08:30.920
Isn't the Legislator

00:08:30.920 --> 00:08:35.410
one of the Underworld's top 
three that we met before?

00:08:36.420 --> 00:08:39.860
So something happened to the Legislator?

00:08:39.860 --> 00:08:41.400
He's hungover, isn't he?

00:08:42.290 --> 00:08:44.290
He wants you two to come.

00:08:43.360 --> 00:08:44.290
Me, too?

00:08:45.000 --> 00:08:49.300
Does he want us to take care of him?

00:08:49.300 --> 00:08:51.300
Well, he didn't say it's a "rule"...

00:08:51.300 --> 00:08:53.860
We're not going to help him?

00:08:53.860 --> 00:08:56.700
There are plenty of other people 
he can ask to take care of him.

00:08:56.700 --> 00:08:58.800
It could be a serious hangover.

00:08:58.800 --> 00:09:01.180
Apparently he's seriously injured.

00:09:01.180 --> 00:09:02.380
What?

00:09:22.800 --> 00:09:25.330
My, my.

00:09:26.020 --> 00:09:27.860
Please, right this way.

00:09:27.860 --> 00:09:29.840
I'll take you to him.

00:09:29.840 --> 00:09:32.780
So this is what it's like on the inside.

00:09:32.780 --> 00:09:36.590
When I came here before, I only 
got to look from the outside.

00:09:34.980 --> 00:09:36.590
Don't look around so much.

00:09:36.590 --> 00:09:38.090
Legislator.

00:09:38.460 --> 00:09:43.140
The master of the Mononokean 
and his employee are here.

00:09:43.140 --> 00:09:44.730
Come in.

00:09:56.380 --> 00:09:58.520
If you'll excuse me.

00:09:58.520 --> 00:10:02.250
Mr. Legislator? Aren't you... injured?

00:10:06.540 --> 00:10:07.680
Hey.

00:10:09.940 --> 00:10:12.540
You arrived at just the right time, Itsuki.

00:10:12.540 --> 00:10:15.400
Could you pack this pipe with tobacco?

00:10:15.400 --> 00:10:17.510
It's a bit tough with one hand.

00:10:17.510 --> 00:10:19.220
He broke a bone?

00:10:22.040 --> 00:10:23.580
Is it broken?

00:10:23.580 --> 00:10:25.140
It's probably broken.

00:10:25.140 --> 00:10:27.890
<i>He's squeezing a broken 
arm as hard as he can!</i>

00:10:28.260 --> 00:10:30.150
Itsuki, the tobacco.

00:10:30.150 --> 00:10:31.080
I refuse.

00:10:31.080 --> 00:10:33.920
Mr. Legislator, what happened to your arm?

00:10:33.920 --> 00:10:36.980
You shouldn't smoke when you're injured.

00:10:36.980 --> 00:10:38.980
At least, humans shouldn't...

00:10:38.980 --> 00:10:43.030
Look, Itsuki. Ashiya-kun is worried about me.

00:10:43.030 --> 00:10:45.620
You may be the master,

00:10:45.620 --> 00:10:49.040
but perhaps there are things you 
could learn from your employee.

00:10:49.440 --> 00:10:52.920
That's such a good lesson, 
I can hardly believe it's coming

00:10:52.920 --> 00:10:55.740
from my superior, who cares 
so little about being a nuisance

00:10:55.740 --> 00:10:58.360
that every time he has a hangover, 
he summons me with an SOS

00:10:58.360 --> 00:11:00.800
and puts my own work behind schedule.

00:11:00.800 --> 00:11:04.050
How verbose. Are you mad?

00:11:04.050 --> 00:11:07.260
You lied about being seriously 
injured to get me to come here!

00:11:07.260 --> 00:11:09.720
This is plenty serious.

00:11:10.960 --> 00:11:15.070
Besides, I'm lucky I wasn't 
more seriously injured.

00:11:15.070 --> 00:11:18.610
I wasn't expecting to be 
attacked out of the blue.

00:11:18.610 --> 00:11:20.160
You were attacked?

00:11:20.160 --> 00:11:22.570
Was someone trying to kill you?

00:11:23.080 --> 00:11:25.080
It was absolutely terrifying...

00:11:25.080 --> 00:11:26.780
Liquor and women, right?

00:11:26.780 --> 00:11:29.560
I didn't know she was a violent drunk.

00:11:29.560 --> 00:11:32.380
But she was really apologetic about it later.

00:11:32.380 --> 00:11:33.710
Cute, right?

00:11:33.710 --> 00:11:37.660
Anyway, as you can see, 
my dominant hand is useless.

00:11:37.660 --> 00:11:40.940
I haven't been able to get much work done.

00:11:40.940 --> 00:11:42.460
So...

00:11:47.350 --> 00:11:50.640
Help me finish this work.

00:11:50.640 --> 00:11:53.000
Get your own employees to do it.

00:11:53.000 --> 00:11:57.500
But I don't want them to find 
out I've been putting it off.

00:11:57.500 --> 00:11:59.000
They'll yell at me.

00:11:59.000 --> 00:12:02.490
Mr. Legislator, is your arm really broken?

00:12:02.490 --> 00:12:06.370
If even you refuse, 
I truly will be at a loss.

00:12:06.370 --> 00:12:09.720
Besides, I'm not asking 
you to do it for free.

00:12:11.320 --> 00:12:15.200
Consider it an urgent 
request for the Mononokean.

00:12:15.200 --> 00:12:17.260
Is this enough?

00:12:17.260 --> 00:12:20.960
Make sure you share it evenly 
with Ashiya-kun and Hairball-kun.

00:12:20.960 --> 00:12:23.020
Th-That's not small change!

00:12:23.020 --> 00:12:27.180
<i>He just grabbed a random amount without 
checking the contents of the drawer.</i>

00:12:27.180 --> 00:12:29.080
We should accept the job!

00:12:29.080 --> 00:12:30.970
What?! Don't be fooled!

00:12:30.970 --> 00:12:33.820
It'd be to help me pay off my debt!

00:12:33.820 --> 00:12:36.780
I don't want to quit my job, 
but I want to pay off my debt!

00:12:36.780 --> 00:12:39.600
That's a splendid attitude, Ashiya-kun.

00:12:39.600 --> 00:12:41.990
Even if Abeno-san won't do it, I will!

00:12:41.990 --> 00:12:46.110
<i>He's not going to quit even 
after he's paid off his debt?</i>

00:12:46.110 --> 00:12:48.660
I appreciate it, Ashiya-kun.

00:12:48.660 --> 00:12:50.240
Hear that, Itsuki?

00:12:50.240 --> 00:12:51.240
Abeno-san!

00:12:57.860 --> 00:13:02.010
This job's deadline is today.

00:13:02.010 --> 00:13:04.630
So this is what he meant by SOS!

00:13:16.920 --> 00:13:21.380
Mr. Legislator, what am I stamping?

00:13:21.380 --> 00:13:22.840
Don't worry about it.

00:13:22.840 --> 00:13:24.150
You're better off not knowing.

00:13:24.150 --> 00:13:26.300
I'm better off not knowing?!

00:13:26.300 --> 00:13:29.530
Just something that would be a slight 
disaster if you made a mistake.

00:13:29.530 --> 00:13:32.380
Wh-What kind of disaster?

00:13:34.320 --> 00:13:35.600
Come in.

00:13:36.540 --> 00:13:38.900
Don't you have guests?

00:13:38.900 --> 00:13:40.220
It's all right.

00:13:41.040 --> 00:13:42.980
I'm back, brother.

00:13:42.980 --> 00:13:44.340
How's your arm?

00:13:44.340 --> 00:13:45.800
Shizuku-chan!

00:13:45.800 --> 00:13:49.360
Oh, it's you guys.

00:13:49.360 --> 00:13:51.840
You came to check on my brother's health?

00:13:51.840 --> 00:13:53.680
Does it look like we're checking on him?

00:13:53.680 --> 00:13:55.840
My arm hurts.

00:13:55.840 --> 00:13:58.580
We actually received an SOS...

00:13:58.580 --> 00:14:00.440
SOS?

00:14:01.940 --> 00:14:04.190
Brother!

00:14:04.190 --> 00:14:07.300
You said you finished all your work!

00:14:07.300 --> 00:14:10.450
I thought you'd scold me if 
I told you I wasn't finished.

00:14:10.450 --> 00:14:13.840
But having you scold me isn't so bad.

00:14:13.840 --> 00:14:16.440
You left this much piled up to do?

00:14:16.440 --> 00:14:20.960
Come back after you've fallen out that 
window and actually broken some bones.

00:14:20.960 --> 00:14:23.720
It really is broken. Probably.

00:14:23.720 --> 00:14:25.760
And stop slacking off.

00:14:25.760 --> 00:14:29.100
I'm tired from signing documents 
with my non-dominant hand.

00:14:29.100 --> 00:14:33.100
Look at that. My handwriting is all squiggly.

00:14:33.100 --> 00:14:34.700
So what?

00:14:34.700 --> 00:14:35.940
Shizuku, please.

00:14:35.940 --> 00:14:38.240
You can't have someone else sign for you.

00:14:38.240 --> 00:14:40.320
It's okay as long as no one finds out.

00:14:40.320 --> 00:14:43.260
I'm having Ashiya-kun stamp my seal o—

00:14:45.400 --> 00:14:47.110
Um...

00:14:47.110 --> 00:14:48.860
What's wrong?

00:14:48.860 --> 00:14:51.180
<i>What an evil expression!</i>

00:14:51.180 --> 00:14:52.660
<i>It's saying "good job!"</i>

00:14:52.660 --> 00:14:54.600
What's wrong, Ashiya?

00:14:54.600 --> 00:14:57.250
Um, it's this.

00:14:57.250 --> 00:15:00.250
I stamped the seal sideways.

00:15:00.680 --> 00:15:03.900
That's all? That's not a problem.

00:15:04.720 --> 00:15:06.620
What a relief.

00:15:06.620 --> 00:15:08.880
<i>Did Abeno-san just tsk me?</i>

00:15:10.740 --> 00:15:13.040
Now I suddenly feel exhausted.

00:15:13.040 --> 00:15:15.480
Let's take a little break, Abeno-san.

00:15:15.480 --> 00:15:17.020
Yes, let's rest.

00:15:17.020 --> 00:15:18.640
Are we going to finish in time?

00:15:18.640 --> 00:15:21.700
How many more of these do I have to stamp?

00:15:21.700 --> 00:15:22.640
I don't know.

00:15:22.640 --> 00:15:24.220
Brother...

00:15:24.220 --> 00:15:26.680
I'll get back to work 
once I finish smoking this.

00:15:27.900 --> 00:15:29.300
Look...

00:15:35.500 --> 00:15:37.290
This isn't good.

00:15:37.290 --> 00:15:38.660
Huh?

00:15:39.760 --> 00:15:42.040
Ashiya-kun, you're done stamping things.

00:15:42.560 --> 00:15:43.380
Huh?

00:15:43.380 --> 00:15:44.420
Did he screw up?

00:15:44.420 --> 00:15:47.860
Shizuku, you'll be the next stamper.

00:15:47.860 --> 00:15:49.000
What?!

00:15:49.000 --> 00:15:50.420
Okay, Ashiya-kun.

00:15:50.420 --> 00:15:52.300
Y-Yes?

00:15:52.300 --> 00:15:56.050
Could you take this scroll to the Executive?

00:15:56.860 --> 00:16:01.280
<i>I haven't met the Executive... 
but that's one of the authority figures</i>

00:16:01.280 --> 00:16:04.190
<i>of the Underworld, 
like the Legislator, right?</i>

00:16:04.580 --> 00:16:07.520
Is that the Executive's scroll?

00:16:07.520 --> 00:16:08.320
Yeah.

00:16:08.320 --> 00:16:11.320
It accidentally got mixed in with mine.

00:16:11.840 --> 00:16:18.200
Ashiya-kun wound up stamping my 
seal on the Executive's scroll.

00:16:18.200 --> 00:16:19.860
So tell him...

00:16:19.860 --> 00:16:24.340
"I accidentally stamped my 
seal on your scroll. Sorry."

00:16:24.340 --> 00:16:27.940
"Also, I'm badly injured, 
so come see me."

00:16:27.940 --> 00:16:29.980
Give him the scroll with that brief message.

00:16:29.980 --> 00:16:32.120
Should the message really be that casual?

00:16:32.120 --> 00:16:34.720
You included a personal message! 
That's not brief!

00:16:34.720 --> 00:16:39.100
Also, ask him, "my deadline 
is tomorrow, right?"

00:16:39.100 --> 00:16:41.700
He casually extended his 
own deadline by a day!

00:16:41.700 --> 00:16:44.320
Won't I get in trouble if I say that?

00:16:44.320 --> 00:16:46.260
You'll be fine.

00:16:46.840 --> 00:16:48.100
Even if we do go,

00:16:48.100 --> 00:16:51.980
we can't enter the Executive's territory 
through the Mononokean without permission.

00:16:51.980 --> 00:16:53.600
It's fine.

00:16:53.600 --> 00:16:56.870
We'll take the Mononokean partway 
there and walk the rest of the way.

00:16:57.260 --> 00:17:01.320
Oh? Itsuki, I need you to stay here.

00:17:01.320 --> 00:17:02.870
There's still work to do.

00:17:02.870 --> 00:17:05.750
I have to go by myself?!

00:17:05.750 --> 00:17:09.900
I'll have the tadpole line show 
you to the Executive's place.

00:17:09.900 --> 00:17:11.500
Don't worry about getting lost.

00:17:11.500 --> 00:17:13.880
What <i>are</i> those tadpoles?!

00:17:13.880 --> 00:17:15.140
Wait, wait, wait!

00:17:15.140 --> 00:17:17.460
I'd still be basically going by myself!

00:17:17.460 --> 00:17:18.980
I can't go alone!

00:17:18.980 --> 00:17:22.270
Are you going to let me walk around 
on my own in this place, Abeno-san?

00:17:23.060 --> 00:17:26.020
I have a previous offense, you know.

00:17:28.520 --> 00:17:32.800
Ashiya-kun, don't try to sway Itsuki.

00:17:32.800 --> 00:17:35.150
Then I'll go with you.

00:17:35.150 --> 00:17:38.120
You can't go, Shizuku. 
You have to stamp things.

00:17:39.820 --> 00:17:40.910
Hairball-kun?

00:17:49.920 --> 00:17:52.660
Okay. I have a job for 
you, too, Hairball-kun.

00:17:52.660 --> 00:17:53.300
Huh?

00:17:53.300 --> 00:17:55.480
Wait. What job are you giving him?

00:17:55.480 --> 00:17:57.680
He'll be escorting Ashiya-kun.

00:17:58.720 --> 00:18:00.300
Hairball-kun says,

00:18:00.700 --> 00:18:04.560
"I'll protect Ashiya-kun and make sure

00:18:04.560 --> 00:18:08.560
he makes it safely to the Executive."

00:18:09.260 --> 00:18:11.400
How dependable.

00:18:11.400 --> 00:18:13.260
Fuzzy!

00:18:13.260 --> 00:18:16.400
<i>Did the hairball really say any of that?</i>

00:18:17.120 --> 00:18:21.160
Anyway, Ashiya-kun, say "hi" 
to the Executive for me.

00:18:47.980 --> 00:18:51.100
We finally found something 
that looks like a path.

00:18:51.100 --> 00:18:53.080
I hope I didn't get my kimono dirty.

00:18:53.080 --> 00:18:55.200
Since I'm borrowing it, 
I'd better be careful.

00:18:57.800 --> 00:19:02.100
<i>—ya-kun? Ashiya-kun? Can... hear me?</i>

00:19:02.100 --> 00:19:03.180
Mr. Legislator?

00:19:03.180 --> 00:19:06.950
<i>Where are... right now?</i>

00:19:06.950 --> 00:19:11.780
We made it through the game trail 
and just came out onto a thin path.

00:19:14.500 --> 00:19:20.160
<i>How much far... to... Executive's place?</i>

00:19:20.160 --> 00:19:23.850
If you keep following the path, 
you'll reach the Birdcage.

00:19:23.850 --> 00:19:25.140
<i>Bird?</i>

00:19:25.140 --> 00:19:27.160
The Birdcage.

00:19:31.280 --> 00:19:36.980
Ashiya-kun, Itsuki says you've 
probably lost the scroll by now.

00:19:36.980 --> 00:19:38.740
<i>Did you lose it already?</i>

00:19:38.740 --> 00:19:40.400
I haven't lost it!

00:19:40.400 --> 00:19:41.990
I have it wrapped around my neck!

00:19:41.990 --> 00:19:42.860
Huh?

00:19:46.320 --> 00:19:48.800
Hello, Mr. Legislator?

00:19:48.800 --> 00:19:50.500
Hello?

00:19:51.560 --> 00:19:54.120
The call dropped...

00:19:56.790 --> 00:19:58.500
What, what, what?! What was that sound?

00:19:58.500 --> 00:20:00.010
There was a rustling noise!

00:20:02.360 --> 00:20:03.620
It's just a bird...

00:20:04.240 --> 00:20:07.390
Right, it's a forest, after all! 
It figures there'd be birds!

00:20:09.760 --> 00:20:14.150
And I've got Fuzzy and the 
tadpole to keep me company.

00:20:14.150 --> 00:20:15.660
I'm not alone.

00:20:15.660 --> 00:20:17.650
It's okay. I'm fine.

00:20:19.400 --> 00:20:22.440
Don't scare me like that, Fuzzy...

00:20:33.410 --> 00:20:37.120
Hello? Mr. Legislator? Abeno-san?

00:20:37.120 --> 00:20:39.300
SOS! SOS!

00:20:41.440 --> 00:20:43.240
It's no use.

00:20:43.240 --> 00:20:46.360
The reception's no good around there.

00:20:49.460 --> 00:20:51.060
Are you that worried about him?

00:20:51.060 --> 00:20:52.900
I'm not worried about him.

00:20:57.920 --> 00:21:02.180
I'm just worried he might do something again.

00:21:02.180 --> 00:21:04.200
He <i>is</i> my employee.

00:21:06.200 --> 00:21:08.700
Hold on! Don't move!

00:21:12.420 --> 00:21:14.210
Um...

00:21:18.560 --> 00:21:20.880
Go right ahead.

00:21:24.590 --> 00:21:28.440
So it wasn't a savage 
beast, just another bird.

00:21:28.440 --> 00:21:30.850
Wait, was that a bird?

00:21:31.260 --> 00:21:35.060
It sounded a little more intense before.

00:21:35.060 --> 00:21:36.350
Must've been my imagination.

00:23:25.000 --> 00:23:39.980
<b>Next time: "The Tail"</b>

00:23:25.800 --> 00:23:28.380
I thought we just came to 
check on the Legislator!

00:23:28.380 --> 00:23:32.800
Why am I stuck on this 
crazy adventure by myself?!

00:23:33.180 --> 00:23:35.260
Next time, "The Tail."

00:23:35.260 --> 00:23:38.720
Save me, Fuzzy!
